    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n971" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγυι-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, a name of Apollo, as <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guardian of the streets and highways</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				631
			</span></i>, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.159
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pointed pillar, set up as his statue</i> or <i>altar</i> at
			the street-door, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				875
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				87
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dieuchid.
				2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγυιεὺς βωμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					370
				</span></i>
			.</div>
